<%# Flash messages.
    role=status/alert so screen readers announce them without a focus change.
    Each carries an icon plus text, so meaning never rests on colour alone.

    Success auto-hides after 6s and errors stay. That split is the whole convention, and it is a
    property of what the message *is* rather than of how it looks: a notice reports that something
    you just did worked, and is worthless a minute later; an alert is often the only record of what
    went wrong, and `role="alert"` interrupts to say so. Nothing else in the app dismisses itself -
    `components/ui/_callout` is page state rather than an outcome, and the error summaries on
    students#new, students#edit and profiles are the same shape as this alert.

    The removal is silent by design: `role="status"` announces the message when it appears, and
    taking it away later is not announced. %>
<% if notice.present? %>
  <div id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite"
       data-controller="auto-dismiss dismiss"
       data-action="mouseenter->auto-dismiss#hold mouseleave->auto-dismiss#start
                    focusin->auto-dismiss#hold focusout->auto-dismiss#start"
       class="mb-4 flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-green-50 border border-green-200 text-green-900 rounded-lg">
    <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
    </svg>
    <p class="text-sm"><span class="font-semibold">Success:</span> <%= notice %></p>
    <%= render "layouts/flash_dismiss", tone: :notice %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<% if alert.present? %>
  <%# No auto-dismiss here, and that is the whole point of the split. It is dismissible, though:
      sticking until the reader clears it is different from sticking until they navigate away, and
      every system that ships an error banner - Primer flash, Polaris Banner with onDismiss, Carbon
      inline notification - lets it be closed. %>
  <div id="alert" role="alert"
       data-controller="dismiss"
       class="mb-4 flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 text-red-900 rounded-lg">
    <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10A8 8 0 112 10a8 8 0 0116 0zm-8-5a.75.75 0 01.75.75v4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.5 0v-4.5A.75.75 0 0110 5zm0 10a1 1 0 100-2 1 1 0 000 2z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
    </svg>
    <p class="text-sm"><span class="font-semibold">Error:</span> <%= alert %></p>
    <%= render "layouts/flash_dismiss", tone: :alert %>
  </div>
<% end %>
